1
00:00:00,806 --> 00:00:02,556
(Leonard:)-What about me?
-I'm sorry, Leonard...

2
00:00:02,725 --> 00:00:07,025
(Sheldon:)...it's too early to discount the possibility
of this being an inside job.

3
00:00:07,188 --> 00:00:10,898
(Leonard:)Would I be completely out of line
to ask you to shoot him?

4
00:00:11,108 --> 00:00:14,278
(Policeman:)I'd be happy to put him under
a 72-hour psychiatric hold.

5
00:00:15,738 --> 00:00:19,028
(Sheldon:)I'm not crazy.
My mother had me tested.

6
00:00:19,242 --> 00:00:22,622
We're done. Call this number,
and we'll fax you a copy of the report.

7
00:00:22,787 --> 00:00:24,867
(Policeman:)You can submit it
to your insurance company.

8
00:00:25,039 --> 00:00:28,329
(Sheldon:)I'm sorry, that's the end
of your inquiry?

9
00:00:28,501 --> 00:00:31,631
(Policeman:)Do you have any more information
that might be relevant?

10
00:00:31,796 --> 00:00:34,386
(Sheldon:)Goodness. Where do I begin?
For instance, my laptop...

11
00:00:34,548 --> 00:00:37,758
(Sheldon:)...contained four out of the five
gedanken experiments necessary...

12
00:00:37,927 --> 00:00:40,097
...for a restatement of
the quantum measurement problem.

13
00:00:40,263 --> 00:00:41,683
How's that going to help them?

14
00:00:41,847 --> 00:00:44,017
(Sheldon:)They could monitor
scientific publications...

15
00:00:44,183 --> 00:00:47,683
(Sheldon:)...and see if anyone posts such
a restatement in the next couple of months.

16
00:00:47,853 --> 00:00:51,693
(Sheldon:)If so, the authors are most likely
in possession of my stolen laptop.

17
00:00:52,817 --> 00:00:55,067
(Policeman:)Good night, fellas.

18
00:00:55,236 --> 00:01:07,026
(Policeman:)Come on, Bochco.

